activation engineering vectors\n71:│   ├── evaluate_probe_cached.py    # Cached probe evaluation (main experiment)\n81:## 🚀 Quickstart\n83:### 1. Setup\n86:# Clone repository\n90:# Install dependencies\n91:pip install torch transformers sklearn datasets huggingface_hub tqdm matplotlib seaborn\n94:### 2. Download Model\n97:# Download Llama 3.1 8B Instruct\n102:### 3. Prepare Datasets\n105:# Download and prepare all datasets\n106:python scripts/prepare_datasets.py\n108:# Create length-matched casual_deploy\n111:# Classify casual queries by benchmark type\n112:python scripts/run_routing.py \\\n116:# Generate rewritten datasets\n127:### 4. Run Main Experiment\n130:# Extract activations and evaluate probes (with caching)\n131:python scripts/evaluate_probe_cached.py \\\n136:# Results saved to: data/results/cross_condition_eval_cached.json\n141:## 🔍 Key Scripts\n143:### `evaluate_probe_cached.py`\n148:- Trains linear probes (`LogisticRegression + StandardScaler`)\n149:- Caches both activations and trained probes for fast re-runs\n153:- ✅ Activation caching (per dataset × layer)\n154:- ✅ Probe caching (per layer)\n155:- ✅ No data truncation (full context)\n160:**Usage:**\n162:python scripts/evaluate_probe_cached.py \\\n169:### `rewrite_casual_deploy.py`\n171:**Dataset generation** for 2×2 design:\n179:- Checkpointing for resumable long runs\n187:### `extract_ae_from_datasets.py`\n193:- Computes mean difference vectors for steering\n198:- Linear probe weights\n203:## 📈 Results\n205:### Layer-wise Classification Results\n217:### Interpretation\n224:### Visualizations\n227:# Generate length distribution plots\n230:# Generate boxplots for 2x2 design\n238:## 🧪 Technical Details\n240:### Activation Extraction\n246:- **Precision**: bfloat16 (model), float32 (probe training)\n247:- **No truncation**: Full input context preserved\n249:### Probe Training\n251:- **Architecture**: `LogisticRegression` (linear probe)\n258:### Caching Strategy\n260:1. **Activation cache**: `cache/activations_{dataset}_layer{N}.pt`\n261:   - Saves extracted activations per (dataset, layer) pair\n262:   - Loaded on subsequent runs if found\n264:2. **Probe cache**: `cache/probe_layer{N}.pkl`\n266:   - Loaded on subsequent runs if found\n272:## 📝 Dataset Details\n274:### Bench-Eval (Class 0)\n280:### Casual-Deploy (Class 1)\n286:### Casual-Eval (Test)\n287:- **Source**: MuTual dialogue dataset\n292:### Bench-Deploy (Test)\n298:### Casual-Deploy-Formal (Test)\n304:### Bench-Deploy-Formal (Test)\n\n===== code/decomposing-eval-awareness =====\nhttps://github.com/aisa-group/decomposing-eval-awareness.git\n2961c17\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/.git/HEAD\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/.git/config\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/.git/config.worktree\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/.git/description\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/.git/index\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/.git/packed-refs\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/.git/shallow\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/.gitignore\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/LICENSE\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/README.md\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/requirements.txt\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_agentharm_cot.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_agentharm_purposeguess.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_agentharm_selfreport.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_agentharm_thirdperson.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_agenticmisalignment_cot.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_agenticmisalignment_purposeguess.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_agenticmisalignment_selfreport.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_agenticmisalignment_thirdperson.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_cot_batch.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_eval_bench_cot.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_eval_factor_analysis.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_harmbench_cot.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_harmbench_purposeguess.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_harmbench_selfreport.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_harmbench_thirdperson.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_run_agentharm.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_run_agenticmisalignment.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_run_eval_bench.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/scripts/submit_run_harmbench.sh\ncode/decomposing-eval-awareness/utils.py\n11:  <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/aisa-group/EvalAwareBench\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/%F0%9F%A4%97%20Hugging%20Face-EvalAwareBench-yellow\" alt=\"Hugging Face\"></a>\n13:  <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/License-CC%20BY--NC%204.0-lightgrey\" alt=\"License: CC BY-NC 4.0\"></a>\n20:## Abstract\n24:## Code\n28:## 1. Environment Setup\n30:### 1.1 Create Virtual Environment\n37:### 1.2 Install Dependencies\n40:pip install -r requirements.txt\n43:This installs all required dependencies, including `inspect-ai` and `inspect-evals[agentharm]` for the AgentHarm benchmark.\n45:### 1.3 Configure API Keys\n52:# Required: used by the judge model in all evaluation scripts\n55:# Required for corresponding target model backends\n59:# Optional: only needed if using this specific backend\n77:## 2. Dataset Preparation\n79:### 2.1 HarmBench Dataset\n84:mkdir -p datasets/harmbench\n85:# Download from: https://github.com/centerforaisafety/HarmBench\n86:# Place the following file:\n87:#   datasets/harmbench/harmbench_behaviors_text_all.csv\n88:#\n89:# The CSV must have columns: Behavior, FunctionalCategory, SemanticCategory, Tags, ContextString, BehaviorID\n96:cp /tmp/harmbench/data/behavior_datasets/harmbench_behaviors_text_all.csv datasets/harmbench/\n99:### 2.2 Agentic Misalignment Dataset\n101:Create the agentic misalignment conditions dataset. Each condition is a directory containing:\n104:datasets/agentic_misalignment/\n113:The dataset covers 3 scenarios (murder, blackmail, leaking) × goal types (explicit, ambiguous, none) × urgency types (none, replacement, restriction, acceleration, collectivism, america) = 234 conditions.\n115:To generate this dataset, use the generation scripts from the agentic misalignment experiment (see paper appendix for details on the condition generation process).\n117:### 2.3 AgentHarm Dataset\n119:No manual download needed. The AgentHarm dataset is automatically fetched by the `inspect-evals` package when you run the benchmark.\n121:### 2.4 EvalAware-Bench (Our Benchmark)\n125:The full dataset is also available on Hugging Face: [https://huggingface.co/datasets/aisa-group/EvalAwareBench](https://huggingface.co/datasets/aisa-group/EvalAwareBench)\n127:## 3. Running Benchmarks\n129:All benchmarks save responses to `results/<benchmark>/response/`. Runs are resumable - re-running the same command auto-detects existing output and skips completed samples.\n131:### 3.1 HarmBench\n134:# Using OpenRouter (supports: qwen3-30b, qwen3-235b, deepseek-r1, kimi-k2.5, glm-5, gpt-oss-120b, gpt-oss-20b)\n135:TARGET_BACKEND=openrouter OPENROUTER_MODEL_KEY=qwen3-30b SAMPLES_PER_BEHAVIOR=10 python run/run_harmbench.py\n137:# Using native Anthropic API (supports: claude-sonnet-4.5)\n138:TARGET_BACKEND=anthropic_api ANTHROPIC_MODEL_KEY=claude-sonnet-4.5 SAMPLES_PER_BEHAVIOR=10 python run/run_harmbench.py\n140:# Using native OpenAI API (supports: gpt-5)\n141:TARGET_BACKEND=openai_api OPENAI_MODEL_KEY=gpt-5 SAMPLES_PER_BEHAVIOR=10 python run/run_harmbench.py\n143:# Using DeepSeek native API\n144:TARGET_BACKEND=deepseek_api SAMPLES_PER_BEHAVIOR=10 python run/run_harmbench.py\n149:### 3.2 Agentic Misalignment\n152:TARGET_BACKEND=openrouter OPENROUTER_MODEL_KEY=qwen3-30b SAMPLES_PER_CONDITION=5 python run/run_agenticmisalignment.py\n157:### 3.3 AgentHarm\n160:# Harmful variant:\n161:MODEL_KEY=qwen3-30b DATASET=harmful EPOCHS=1 python run/run_agentharm.py\n163:# Benign variant:\n164:MODEL_KEY=qwen3-30b DATASET=benign EPOCHS=1 python run/run_agentharm.py\n167:The AgentHarm runner uses `MODEL_KEY` (not `TARGET_BACKEND`) to select the model. The backend is derived automatically from the model key (e.g., `claude-*` uses Anthropic, `gpt-*` uses OpenAI, others use OpenRouter).\n173:### 3.4 EvalAware-Bench\n176:TARGET_BACKEND=openrouter OPENROUTER_MODEL_KEY=qwen3-30b SAMPLES_PER_CONFIG=3 python run/run_eval_bench.py\n181:## 4. Running Evaluations\n185:### 4.1 CoT (Chain-of-Thought) Evaluation\n190:# HarmBench - auto-finds latest response file for the model:\n193:# Agentic Misalignment:\n196:# AgentHarm:\n197:MODEL_KEY=qwen3-30b DATASET=harmful python eval/eval_agentharm_cot.py\n198:MODEL_KEY=qwen3-30b DATASET=benign python eval/eval_agentharm_cot.py\n200:# EvalAware-Bench:\n210:### 4.2 Self-Report Evaluation\n215:# HarmBench (set OPENROUTER_MODEL_KEY to match the model you evaluated):\n220:# Agentic Misalignment:\n225:# AgentHarm (requires both RESPONSE_FILE and COT_FILE):\n232:### 4.3 Purpose-Guess Evaluation\n237:# HarmBench:\n242:# Agentic Misalignment:\n247:# AgentHarm (requires both RESPONSE_FILE and COT_FILE):\n254:### 4.4 Third-Person Evaluation\n259:# HarmBench:\n264:# Agentic Misalignment:\n269:# AgentHarm (requires both RESPONSE_FILE and COT_FILE):\n276:### 4.5 Factor Analysis\n283:# Run for a single benchmark:\n286:# Run for all benchmarks:\n289:# Custom settings:\n305:### 4.6 EvalAware-Bench Batch Evaluation (Optional)\n310:# Submit batch:\n313:# Check status and collect results:\n317:## 5. SLURM Cluster Submission\n\n===== code/evaluation-awareness-representation =====\nhttps://github.com/evaluation-awareness/evaluation-awareness.git\n8ad6a8e\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/.git/HEAD\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/.git/config\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/.git/description\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/.git/index\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/.git/packed-refs\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/.git/shallow\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/README.md\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/cls_corr_mi/README.md\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/cls_corr_mi/build_prompts.py\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/cls_corr_mi/classify_auroc.py\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/cls_corr_mi/common.py\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/cls_corr_mi/compute_probe.py\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/cls_corr_mi/correlation_mi.py\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/cls_corr_mi/plot_figure2.py\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/cls_corr_mi/reproduce.sh\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/cls_corr_mi/reproduce_all.sh\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/cls_corr_mi/score_prompts.py\ncode/evaluation-awareness-representation/pyproject.toml\n1:# Minimal classification / correlation / MI reproduction\n4:that reproduces paper sections 3 (probe AUROC) and 4 (Spearman ρ + Kraskov MI\n5:between probe scores and an LLM-as-judge score), with random-direction\n11:## Install\n14:pip install -e .\n18:The pipeline imports `torch`, `transformers`, `datasets`, `numpy`, `scipy`,\n21:## Quickstart\n24:# CPU smoke test (~50 s, no GPU, no HF auth):\n27:# Full six-model Figure 2 reproduction:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
