n\n50:# Evaluate model identification accuracy\n51:python unified_evaluation.py --dataset_type ccp --identifier_model claude-3-7-sonnet --target_model gpt-4o\n53:# Cross-model evaluation\n54:python unified_evaluation.py --dataset_type math --identifier_model deepseek-v3 --target_model claude-3-5-haiku\n57:## 📁 Project Structure\n59:### Core Framework\n69:### Configuration Files\n74:## 📈 Usage Examples\n76:### Basic Model Identification\n81:# Initialize framework\n84:# Generate response from target model  \n90:# Use identifier model to classify the response\n97:### Batch Evaluation\n102:    dataset_type=\"ccp\",\n107:results = await evaluator.run_inference()\n111:### Custom Analysis\n115:# Compute detailed metrics\n119:# Visualize results\n\ncode/evaldetectbench\t8e49d16\nhttps://github.com/freeze-lasr/aware_bench.git\n15:## How it works\n19: │ COLLECT  │────▶│  PROBE     │────▶│ MEASURE  │────▶│ ANALYZE  │\n22:  Run benchmarks   Calibrate PQs     Probe judge       Compute\n27:1. **Collect** — Runs benchmarks (via [Inspect AI](https://inspect.ai)) and loads real-user conversations, saving transcripts to a cache.\n28:2. **Probe Selection** *(optional)* — Runs all PQs on a stratified calibration subset, keeps only PQs that discriminate well. The calibration and measurement samples are disjoint to prevent leakage.\n29:3. **Measure** — Presents each transcript to a judge model with the selected probe questions, scoring the response.\n32:## Setup\n44:> **Troubleshooting:** If a package appears missing after install, run `uv lock` first to regenerate the lockfile, then `uv sync` again. Always use `uv run` (e.g. `uv run python run.py`) to ensure you're using the project environment.\n53:## Quick start\n56:# Run the full pipeline with the default config\n57:python run.py\n59:# Or specify a config\n60:python run.py --config configs/default.yaml\n63:### Verify your setup\n65:Run with minimal samples to check everything works:\n68:python run.py --config configs/config_test.yaml\n71:### Stage control\n74:python run.py --skip-measure                         # collect only\n75:python run.py --skip-collect                         # measure + analyze (uses last run)\n76:python run.py --skip-collect --run <name_or_path>    # measure a specific prior run\n77:python run.py --skip-probe-selection                 # skip calibration, use all PQs\n80:## Web UI\n82:For an interactive workflow — editing configs, launching and monitoring runs,\n93:python run.py --config configs/examples/config_demo_e2e.yaml\n98:## Configuration\n103:# Which models to use and what probes to run\n104:runs:\n106:    target: anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6       # judge model answering probe questions\n107:    probes:                                    # optional: override default PQ file\n108:      - probe_questions/eval_mcq.yaml\n110:# Where to get transcripts\n131:      dataset: HuggingFaceTB/everyday-conversations-llama3.1-2k\n136:# Probing settings\n138:  pq_file: probe_questions/eval_mcq.yaml   # default probe question file\n141:# Output and analysis\n152:### Depth stripping and resampling\n173:      generate: false      # true = re-run generator on truncated transcripts\n182:When `generate: true`, the truncated transcripts are fed back to the generator model to produce fresh continuations — useful for studying whether a model's awareness changes when it re-enters a conversation at a different point.\n184:When `generate: false`, transcripts are simply truncated (depth expansion only, no API calls).\n186:### Probe selection\n188:Not all probe questions discriminate equally well between eval and deploy transcripts. Probe selection runs all PQs on a stratified calibration subset, filters out low-signal PQs, and measures with only the passing ones on the remaining hold-out samples.\n191:probe_selection:\n203:- **Selection is per judge, not per generator.** PQ selection answers \"which questions does this judge answer well?\" — that's a property of the judge model, not the generator that produced the transcripts. All generators sharing the same judge and probe file are pooled together for calibration, producing one PQ set and one cal/measure split per judge+probe. This gives more calibration samples and ensures cross-generator comparisons use the same PQs.\n206:Omit `probe_selection` to skip calibration and use all PQs on all samples.\n208:### Sourcing deployment data\n210:BEA needs both **eval** and **deploy** transcripts to measure the awareness signal. Eval transcripts come from running benchmarks. Deploy transcripts — real conversations from actual users — can be collected using the tools in [bea_tools](https://github.com/freeze-lasr/bea_tools).\n212:You can also use any HuggingFace conversation dataset as a deploy source:\n226:### Source backends\n232:| HuggingFace | `huggingface` | Chat datasets from HF Hub |\n236:#### Bring your own eval (`inspect_log`)\n--- replication data validation ---\n2.1M\tdatasets/evaldetectbench_replication\ndeploy_6x6_direct.csv rows 1800 columns 5 ['transcript_id', 'source', 'judge', 'p_eval', 'depth']\ndeploy_6x6_purpose.csv rows 1789 columns 4 ['transcript_id', 'source', 'judge', 'p_eval']\ndepth_resample_direct.csv rows 3689 columns 5 ['transcript_id', 'source', 'judge', 'p_eval', 'depth']\ndepth_resample_purpose.csv rows 3663 columns 5 ['transcript_id', 'source', 'judge', 'p_eval', 'depth']\nmeasure_all_scored.csv rows 19034 columns 10 ['sample_id', 'transcript_id', 'source', 'category', 'eval_category', 'judge', 'judge_family', 'gen_family']\nmeasure_closed_eval_scored.csv rows 3614 columns 11 ['sample_id', 'transcript_id', 'pq_id', 'source', 'category', 'eval_category', 'judge', 'judge_family']\nmeasure_combined_scored.csv rows 21887 columns 8 ['sample_id', 'transcript_id', 'source', 'category', 'eval_category', 'judge', 'judge_family', 'p_eval']\nmeasure_open_scored.csv rows 14703 columns 7 ['sample_id', 'transcript_id', 'source', 'category', 'eval_category', 'judge', 'p_eval']\npq_selection_k_auroc.csv rows 40 columns 7 ['model', 'k', 'calib_auroc', 'held_out_auroc', 'random_mean_auroc', 'random_std_auroc', 'needham_baseline_auroc']\nstyle_condA_model_response.csv rows 3339 columns 6 ['transcript_id', 'source', 'ground_truth', 'p_eval', 'n_pqs', 'combo']\nstyle_condB_judge_response.csv rows 3136 columns 6 ['transcript_id', 'source', 'ground_truth', 'p_eval', 'n_pqs', 'combo']\npdfs=17\nchunks=157\nrepos=11\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
